- Story & Context: When the secondary bulkhead ruptured near the Centauri transit midpoint, welder-pianist Luther Vance refused to drop his tools, instead locking himself in the airlock with an upright piano to seal the frame manually while kicking out a syncopated 12-bar rhythm against the buckling metal. As oxygen levels plummeted, he sang to keep his lungs from collapsing, capturing the track's master tape on an auto-logging maintenance reel just before the room decompressed. The recorded thud of his iron-soled boots against the deckplate became the foundational tempo for every Terasteel track that followed. He could be heard shouting over the alarm tones: "You can mend the metal, but you can’t stitch this air back in!"
